            <h2>5. Logistics and Shipping</h2>
            <p>
              Common Incoterms: <strong>FOB</strong> (Factory delivers to departure port – most common),{' '}
              <strong>EXW</strong> (Buyer arranges all shipping from factory door), <strong>CIF</strong> (Factory pays
              freight and insurance to destination port).
            </p>
            <p>
              Inflatable products are low-weight, high-volume – volumetric weight (DIM) often determines shipping cost.
              Request vacuum-packed packaging to reduce volume by 50–60%. Sea freight from China to EU: 25–35 days; to
              US West Coast: 15–20 days.
            </p>

            <h2>6. Common Pitfalls</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <strong>No factory audit:</strong> Always perform or commission a third-party audit (QIMA, SGS, Bureau
                Veritas)
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Verbal specs only:</strong> Detailed technical specification sheet signed by both parties
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Skipping sample approval:</strong> Written sign-off on samples before bulk production
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>No QC during production:</strong> Third-party inspection during production (DUPRO) and before
                shipment (PSI)
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Ignoring compliance:</strong> Verify CE/UKCA certification before production
              </li>
            </ul>

            <h2>7. Why Aquafarer</h2>
            <p>
